gocpp ocpp-go compatibility module
==================================

This module (github.com/shiv3/gocpp/compat/ocppgo) provides the public API of
github.com/lorenzodonini/ocpp-go, so that an application can switch to the gocpp
runtime with one `replace` line. It declares the module path
github.com/lorenzodonini/ocpp-go because Go requires a replacement module to
declare the path it replaces.

Upstream
--------

A large part of this directory is a copy of ocpp-go, which is
Copyright (c) the ocpp-go authors and licensed under the MIT License (see
LICENSE, the upstream text, unchanged). The pinned source is recorded in
UPSTREAM (tag and commit). That source is the fork line v0.17.2-fix.x of
https://github.com/lorenzodonini/ocpp-go.

What is changed
---------------

- Every difference between the pinned upstream files and the files in this
  directory is a patch in patches/. scripts/sync-upstream.sh re-creates the
  upstream files from the pinned tag and applies the patches; with --check it
  verifies that this tree is exactly that. CI runs the check.
- Files that exist only here (they are not in upstream and have no patch) carry
  a "gocpp" header: ocppj/server_gocpp.go, ws/server.go, everything under
  internal/compatrt and compat/, and the scripts. They are licensed under the
  gocpp MIT license (LICENSE.gocpp).
- ws/*_test.go of upstream (white-box tests of the gorilla based server) are
  removed by a patch; ws/blackbox_test.go replaces them.
- Everything else (ocpp, ocpp1.6, ocpp2.0.1, logging, internal/callbackqueue,
  example, the upstream tests) is an unmodified copy.
